{
  "requirement": "The harness MUST construct each assessment's mandatory input set by combining\nthe contributions specified by the requirements applicable to that subject and\nits inputs. A requirement that contributes inputs MUST cite this requirement and\ndefine which sources it contributes and when. The harness MUST include every\napplicable contribution, deduplicate identical selections, and report\nunresolvable mandatory inputs before inference. The complete set MUST be supplied\nin the initial model request.\nA file selected as a mandatory input MUST be visible under\n{cite}`requirements.sdk.sources.local_provider`. A denied selection MUST abort\nunder {cite}`requirements.authoring.read_denial.mandatory`.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The reviewed tests adequately check `requirements.authoring.mandatory_inputs`. I judged this from the supplied test sources and did not request implementation source.\n\n**Combining every applicable contribution** (the harness MUST combine contributions and include every applicable one):\n- `src/authoring/inputs.rs#mod[tests]/fn[bundle_combines_direct_references_terms_and_current_existing_selectors]` checks the combined set for a requirement subject. It covers the subject's declaration, a cited requirement, cited terms, `{test}` items and examples, and it checks the examples' own bundles. It also checks that a distant requirement, an `{impl}` item and the parent `impl` are left out.\n- `fn[only_edges_leaving_the_subject_contribute_inputs]` checks which edges contribute. Edges leaving the subject do, and edges arriving at it do not. It checks this for requirement, example and parent subjects.\n- `fn[anchored_files_contribute_root_node_inputs]` and `fn[test_anchors_supply_only_the_selected_node]` check anchors. They assert exact input JSON or the selected node only, and that unrelated siblings are absent from the prompt.\n- `fn[references_contribute_their_owning_outline_nodes]` checks Markdown sections, plain-text files and `{fixme}` metadata.\n- `fn[generated_evidence_references_are_omitted_by_default]` checks which files are excluded.\n- `fn[mandatory_inputs_can_read_untracked_declarations_and_terms]` checks untracked declarations and terms.\n- `fn[earlier_evidence_inputs_and_judgments_are_not_carried_forward]` and `fn[unresolvable_earlier_inputs_do_not_block_reassessment]` check that earlier evidence does not contribute.\n- Other subject kinds are covered in `src/authoring/mod.rs`:\n  - citation reviews: `fn[citation_reviews_use_their_prompt_and_record_the_item_and_citations]`\n  - book commentary: `fn[book_commentary_reviews_supply_the_whole_passage_and_check_concordance]`\n  - site reviews: `fn[site_reviews_use_their_prompt_and_record_applies_and_the_site]`\n\n**Deduplicating identical selections:**\n- `fn[citation_review_inputs_combine_item_declarations_terms_and_built_ins_once]` asserts that a doubly cited requirement, a shared term and a duplicated built-in each appear exactly once, and that the set has exactly 5 entries.\n- The bundle test asserts exactly 2 definitions, although the term `terms.unit` is reachable by more than one path.\n- The CLI test in `tests/authoring_cli.rs` asserts that a repeated read is recorded once.\n\n**Complete set in the initial model request:**\n- `fn[citation_reviews_use_their_prompt_and_record_the_item_and_citations]` asserts that the first prompt contains the mandatory hash and the cited text.\n- The test-anchor test asserts the same for the selected node.\n- The `ollama_cli_...` CLI test parses the \"# Mandatory inputs\" section of the first request. It checks that the section contains the requirement, the definition text and the test item, and that it omits the implementation.\n- The tools test `model_inputs_reads_searches_and_citation_prompts_are_redacted` checks what reaches the prompt.\n\n**Visibility under `requirements.sdk.sources.local_provider`, and aborting on denial under `requirements.authoring.read_denial.mandatory`:**\n- `fn[disallowed_mandatory_inputs_abort_preparation]` covers a gitignored declaration. It asserts `PermissionDenied` and that the error names the path.\n- `fn[unreadable_or_denied_anchors_fail_before_inference]` covers a missing file, a missing node and an ignored directory.\n- `fn[evidence_anchors_and_aliases_follow_project_ignore_rules]` covers an ignored directory and a symlink alias.\n- `tools.rs#fn[mandatory_inputs_outside_the_project_still_abort]` covers a path outside the project.\n- The citation test covers a gitignored term file.\n- The CLI test `unresolvable_mandatory_inputs_fail_before_any_model_request` covers the end-to-end abort. The command fails, stderr names the path, the model endpoint is never contacted, and the evidence file is unchanged. This checks that unresolvable inputs are reported before inference.\n\n**Not tested here:** the sentence requiring any contributing requirement to cite this requirement and define its sources is a book-authoring obligation on other requirements. Each of those requirements carries its own tests, and those tests cite this requirement. Batch behavior belongs to the cited `read_denial.mandatory` requirement, which I did not reassess.\n\nI found no plausible requirement-violating behavior that these tests would accept.",
  "references": "24022a85373a405b0fb3408b99edf1d1bbc96fd33788256d087c885bb430c4d7",
